% lib/lists.le — building a list one item at a time, as LE templates.
%
% LE writes a list whole (`[1, 2, 3]`) and asks whether something is in one
% (`*V1* is in *V2*`, language.md §7). A rule that collects things one by one
% — the payments of a loan, from the first to the last, each from the one
% before — also needs to put an item in front of a list it already has.
% A library, not syntax: include it as a resource (a translator copies it
% beside the program it writes, with lists.pl), and use its templates like
% any other.

the knowledge base lists includes these resources:
    lists.pl.

the templates are:
    *a list* is *an item* followed by *a second list*.

the knowledge base lists includes:

% Every template is answered by lists.pl.
